    "details": {
      "cr": 8,
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "",
        "swarm": "med"
      },
      "alignment": "Neutral",
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>The people of Greenrest, come to stop the party at the tree.</strong> They are neighbours, not soldiers: farmhands, shopkeepers, grandmothers and boys, frightened of losing everything the Dreamer's summer has given them. They heard her ask to be freed, the same as everyone, and came anyway. Warin's militia fights behind them.</p><p><strong>Kill or knock out.</strong> On any melee hit, the attacker chooses whether the townsfolk it drops are killed or knocked out. Ranged attacks and spells can only kill. Tell the table before initiative.</p><p><strong>Aftermath.</strong> Keep a tally of lethal damage beside the HP bar: roughly one dead neighbour per 20 lethal damage. That is how many graves Coll digs.</p><p><strong>Sessions:</strong> 09 · Conclusion (the battle of the square).</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
